@techreport{Wilson,
abstract = {Panel Abstract Data-based solutions are becoming increasingly necessary for the power system of the future. "Data" captured on the power grid is no longer constrained to SCADA, protection, and simple metering. Systems today are becoming increasingly complex, moving away from the traditional one-way generation, transmission, and distribution pipeline. As the grid becomes less centralized, our reliance on data grows; however, little attention has been given to ensuring that said data is of "high quality". Several corrupting influences are responsible for imperfections in data, ranging from relatively simple problems such as missing values, communication bandwidth constraints, and signal processing, among others; to uncertainty in the measurement apparatus itself. This panel will examine some of these challenges, and how they impact data-based applications for the grid.},
