@techreport{Chen2021d,
abstract = {While shipping remains the most fuel-efficient mode of transport, ships emit a significant amount of greenhouse gas (GHG) worldwide. Recent heavy weather-related accidents involving the loss of thousands of containers overboard and ships sinking have created far-reaching environmental damage. Unfortunately, while weather forecasting, computing, and communications technologies have improved significantly, the effectiveness of weather routing still lags behind as it evolves into voyage optimization for efficiency and safety. This paper provides a critical review of the art and science of voyage optimization from the user's holistic points of view. The choices of technologies to address these issues depend on ship type, trade routes, service requirements, charter party agreements, and other operational objectives. To assist the shoreside manager's and ship mas-ter's decision-making process, a risk-based route selection tool utilizing ensemble forecast is proposed along with a list of recommendations for future developments.},
