@article{Lekakou2018a,
abstract = {Short Sea shipping (SSS) has been the main mode of intra-Europe maritime transport. Since 1999 the European Commission has issued various regulations and activities aiming at the promotion of SSS across Europe, due to the mode's high environmental performance and the removal of significant traffic volumes from European roads. Due to the nature of SSS, there is a difficulty to determine activity's concrete boundaries, in terms of markets, services or size of vessels. This complexity generates multiple obstacles both at the collection of dedicated data and the determination of markets' characteristics. Short sea shipping in Greece: Data, impact and challenges 132 IAME 2018 Conference, September 11 th-14 th , Mombasa, Kenya 2 SSS represents almost 77% of goods transported by sea in Greece. However, there is a significant knowledge gap about the characteristics of the sector. The study aims at analyzing the quantitative and qualitative characteristics of the Greek SSS sector. First section provides SSS definitions to pinpoint the special nature of the activity, section two reviews the key obstacles of SSS in EU, while section three presents the main findings of the statistical analysis of the Greek SSS sector. Final section discusses policy considerations for the improvement of the competitiveness of the national sector},
