abstract = {This paper presents a study into the utilization of the non-parametric statistic combined with the Bayesian paradigm for solar irradiance conditions clustering. A Dirichlet-multinomial mixture model is applied to automatically adapt to the correct complexity level and size of the model, and therefore, fit complex probability functions. Posterior computation relies on a numerical procedure based on Markov Chain Monte-Carlo algorithm. Experiments were conducted using three years of solar irradiance data carried out in Rabat, capital of Morocco (34oN latitude, 6o50'W longitude) with a sampling-rate of 6-min. The authors of this work are big supporters of open-source codes, therefore, all methods presented in this manuscript is openly available as a downloadable R-package from https://github.com/frimane/SolMultinomClass.},
