@techreport{,
abstract = {Project Overview The Solar Forecast Arbiter 1 is an open-source evaluation framework for solar forecasting. The framework enables evaluations of solar irradiance, solar power, and net-load forecasts that are impartial, repeatable and auditable. The Solar Forecast Arbiter addresses stakeholder-informed use cases 2 including evaluation of forecast skill, comparisons to reference data sets, private forecast trials, and evaluation of probabilistic forecast skill. The framework includes a data validation toolkit 3 , reference data sources 4 , data privacy protocols 5 , and benchmark forecast capabilities 6 for intra-hour and day ahead forecast horizons. Reports and metrics 7 communicate the relative merits of the test and benchmark forecasts. The reports are created from standardized templates and include graphics for qualitatively evaluating deterministic and probabilistic forecasts and standard metrics for quantitatively evaluating forecasts. The Solar Forecast Arbiter is designed to support all solar forecasting stakeholders, including Solar Forecasting 2 Topic Area 2 and Topic Area 3 teams. Project Goal Our project goal is to develop, demonstrate, test, and deploy an accessible, extensible, open-source framework that enables evaluations of irradiance, solar power, and net-load forecasts that are impartial, repeatable, and auditable (Figure 1). This framework provides reference data and a repeatable, traceable, and transparent set of benchmark forecasts against which forecast skill can be measured over time. Our framework facilitates evaluations of candidate forecast accuracy and skill across the community of forecast users: utilities, transmission system operators, balancing authorities, generation fleet operators, and system aggregators. Forecast users are able to tailor evaluations to address specific interests in terms of forecasted quantities, geographic location, forecast horizons, and temporal and spatial resolution. 1 https://forecastarbiter.epri.com 2},
file = {:C\:/Users/Mhdella/AppData/Local/Mendeley Ltd./Mendeley Desktop/Downloaded/Yuniartika - 2022 - Open Source Evaluation Framework for Solar Forecasging.pdf:pdf},
