@techreport{,
abstract = {1.1 Purpose and objectives The purpose of this project is to further develop current prototype to a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) and industrialize the solution, at the end of this project. The main objective of the product is to reduce emissions from marine commercial short sea vessels, e.g. transport ferries, by guiding the operator toward Green Operation. This assist function, Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based decision making, will show best operational sweet spot for environment, comfort of passengers and time of arrival based on large amount of operational data. The product, a data-based service, will use AI technologies to identify operations, use real-time data and categorize the operations. The current prototype is based on off-the-shelf hardware with simplified software. The first prototype showed a potential for significant fuel (10-35%) and emission reduction for marine commercial segment with a potential to create a sustainable business. However, in order to make a positive business case out of this idea, part of commissioning, software adjustment to operation and maintenance needs to be automated using AI technologies. To this end, the project will drive research on AI for aware systems, and to develop novel machine learning methods and decision support tools that improve operational efficiency and reduce inappropriate use of complex equipment. A successful product will lead into significantly shortening resource training time (currently years of experience needed) hence moving toward a resource efficiency for this segment. This project aims to strengthen partnership between business segment and research in Sweden in AI and climate change for marine segment. Outcome of this project should also help authorities to define new ways of measuring and enforcing commitment to emission targets in marine commercial segment. 1.2 State of the art There are many operational assistance functions available for different transportation segments, from aviation to off-road application. These assist functions, sometimes also controlling the operation, will help the operator to make a safe and sustainable decision based on the input of the system. The model behind the suggestions used to be based on physical models but with advancement in data science and AI, the suggestions in these systems can be based on history of operation of the same system. While the physical},
