abstract = {The paper suggests a three-dimensional graph model for a spatio-temporal representation of a water area with drifting ice objects. The article considers multi-objective route optimization with both additive and minimax criteria. The algorithmic solution of multi-objective optimization is proposed for a set of objective functions, which correspond to the following route parameters: the route length, risks along the route and the number of course direction changes. The method presented in the paper allows finding a set of Pareto-optimal solutions. The paper suggests the algorithm for arranging three-dimensional graph in relation to motion laws of ice objects existing in the considered water area. For illustrating the method, the article provides a computational example of path optimization. The paper also includes the discussion on the parameters influencing computational complexity of practical implementation of the developed method as well as on the approach in general. The developed model can be implemented in designing marine transportation systems and navigation assisting in ice infested water areas.},
